  "subtitle": "caramelised plum rounds on a soft, buttery sponge",
  "excerpt": "An upside-down cake is baked with the fruit arranged in caramelised butter and sugar at the base of the tin, then inverted to serve so the fruit becomes the glossy, jewelled top. Plums work particularly well in this format: their tartness cuts through the buttery caramel, and when halved and arranged cut-side down, they create a striking pattern once the cake is turned out. The sponge base is a moist, tender butter cake that needs no adornment.",
