  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "An upside-down cake needs a tin with a solid base, not a loose-bottomed one: the caramel will seep through a removable base and burn on the oven shelf. Melt the butter and brown sugar directly in the tin if it is ovenproof, or in a small pan and pour into the tin. Arrange the plum halves cut-side down in the caramel before pouring the sponge batter on top."
          }
        ]
      },
